  "result": {
    "summary": "A self-contained dual-contract deployment bundle was derived without changing learned tensors. Across 4,096 reachable states, source and bundle logits were bit-exact and both greedy and sampled actions matched 4,096/4,096. Two four-hand mock sessions produced 29 decisions; journal, raw-hand evidence, two-artifact frozen identity, disjoint token chains, and independent CLI replay all passed. Full suite: 236 passed.",
    "conclusion": "The strongest seed0 12k six-objective MGDA policy is deployable under the exact journaled CPU contract. The missing architecture fields in the continuation checkpoint were repaired transparently through a hash-bound, weight-identical deployment bundle. This is contract evidence, not poker-strength evidence.",
